ExecReason.description:
Why an exec is `failed` or `terminated`:
- `sandbox_terminated`: the sandbox ended (or was ending) first;
- `timeout`: the exec's `timeout` was reached;
- `agent_unavailable`: the sandbox didn't confirm the start in time;
- `cancelled`: killed with `SIGKILL` before its start was confirmed. If the start had in fact reached the sandbox, the exec moves on to what really ran, then exits from the kill;
- `agent_error`: the sandbox returned an inconsistent answer.
